#!/bin/bash
# Wrapper that forces SMPlayer to always open tiled-right.
#
# Editing smplayer.ini's [default_gui] pos=/size= (tried first, 2026-09-18)
# never actually worked: native Wayland deliberately does not let client
# apps set their own absolute window position at all (a real protocol/
# security restriction, not a missing setting) - confirmed via screenshot
# showing the window landing left-of-center regardless of what pos= said.
# Size hints are unreliable too since the WM can override them anyway once
# tiled. The only thing that actually works is triggering GNOME's own
# native tiling (Mutter), the same as pressing Super+Right by hand - which
# requires a REAL simulated key event (below the Wayland client sandbox),
# not anything requestable from inside the app itself. ydotool (+ ydotoold,
# set up 2026-09-18 via a systemd override granting this user's uid/gid
# socket access - see /etc/systemd/system/ydotool.service.d/override.conf)
# provides that.
#
# single_instance_enabled=true in smplayer.ini (flipped 2026-09-20, tested
# working) - a second launch now reconnects to whatever's already running
# instead of spawning a second CPU-heavy decode process (was causing
# system-wide beach-balling with multiple videos left open at once). This
# is safe for tiling specifically because the existing window is already in
# its correct tiled position - reconnecting to load a new file into it
# doesn't move or re-map the window, so there's nothing to re-tile anyway.
# NOT forcing -platform wayland (tried 2026-09-28, reverted same day):
# this machine's smplayer.ini has driver\vo=x11 (the legacy X11-embedded
# video output), which needs a real XWayland X11 window to draw into.
# Forcing native Wayland broke it - fell back to a generic look, likely
# not rendering video via that path at all. Zoom/rotate/flip apparently
# depend on vo=x11, which depends on XWayland - the native-Wayland
# decoration plugin isn't compatible with that setup. Shelved per user
# 2026-09-28 rather than chase a different vo driver right now.
env QT_STYLE_OVERRIDE=Fusion FM_QT_THEME="$HOME/.config/fm-tweaks/qt-theme-smplayer.conf" LD_PRELOAD="$HOME/.themes/qt-fm/libqt-fm.so:$HOME/.themes/qt-noicons/libqt-noicons.so" "$HOME/.local/opt/smplayer-qt6/bin/smplayer" "$@" &
SMPLAYER_PID=$!

# Tiling right is done by the custom-gestures extension (SMPlayerTileRight, direct placement). The old ydotool tile-right chord (Alt+Super+Right)
# was removed 2026-10-26: it left the XWayland client half-active (dead shortcuts, stuck traffic lights, ignored drops).

wait "$SMPLAYER_PID"
